{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016ehSNPa41wmMsA6SjScDZs","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t+++\n2\tid = \"WI-579\"\n3\ttitle = \"The verdict carrier and the adjudication_review dial: gate over logged rounds, tree-bound trailer, generated rollup\"\n4\tworkstream = \"process\"\n5\tspecref = \"\"\n6\tbuildtier = \"strong\"\n7\tpriority = 9\n8\tsafety_class = \"ordinary\"\n9\tsupersedes = \"WI-558;WI-559;WI-560\"\n10\t+++\n11\t\n12\t## Deliverable\n13\t\n14\tThe merge gate reads the EVIDENCE and the evidence names the tree it judged.\n15\t\n16\t`kitlib/verdict.py` (LLR-207, IF-175) is the verdict record's one home: the\n17\tnon-record tree identity — a SHA-256 fold of `git ls-tree -r` with\n18\t`docs/reviews/`, `docs/log.d/` and `docs/iteration/` dropped — the\n19\t`Review-Verdict: APPROVE|CHANGES-REQUESTED rounds=<N> tree=<64 hex>` trailer\n20\tgrammar, the round-file / session-log join, and the branch-scoped readers. Two\n21\tcallers stand on it and that is the point: `integrate._verdict_gate` (may this\n22\tmerge?) and `agent_loop.review_owed_by_evidence` (does this lane still owe a\n23\tround?) asked one question with two rules over two exclusion sets, and the gap\n24\tbetween them drew two identical rounds on WI-547.\n25\t\n26\t- **WI-558 DW1** — the gate computes over the branch's own round files,\n27\t  restricted to rounds a LOGGED reviewer session produced: a file under\n28\t  `docs/reviews/` is a round only when the coordinator's own committed session\n29\t  log for that (train, ordinal) declares a REVIEW phase. Finding K closed —\n30\t  an implementer cannot author its own approval without also forging the loop's\n31\t  telemetry.\n32\t- **WI-558 DW2** — the machine half rides the round's own record commit as a\n33\t  trailer, written by the COORDINATOR and verified against its carrier's tree\n34\t  (the `Bar-Green` pattern). GOVERNING = TREE IDENTITY: a verdict counts only\n35\t  while it names the branch's current non-record tree, read at the WORK TIP so\n36\t  the station refresh still does not stale an honest APPROVE. The freshness\n37\t  comparison is gone; there is no ordering rule left. The trailer is a\n38\t  CROSS-CHECK and never an accept path — one that contradicts the rounds\n39\t  refuses the merge.\n40\t- **WI-558 DW3** — `gen_verdict_rollup.py` (LLR-208) rebirths the rollup as a\n41\t  GENERATED artifact: `docs/stack.ini [generated]`, `trunk_step.py --regen`, a\n42\t  `check.py verdict-rollup` freshness step on the hook floor and in\n43\t  `_TRUNK_FRESHNESS_STEPS`, and `--check` with two answers. The gate never reads\n44\t  it, and the file says so where a human will see it.\n45\t- **WI-558 DW4** — the migration window: the gate accepts EITHER the round\n46\t  evidence or a legacy hand-authored rollup, judged by the SAME identity rule,\n47\t  warning on stderr whenever the legacy path is what cleared it. Two\n48\t  `RESYNC_PACK.md` entries. The trailer is additive and costs an adopter nothing.\n49\t- **WI-558 DW5 / WI-560 DW4 / WI-559 DW3** — `tests/test_verdict_record.py`\n50\t  drives each half beside its opposite (TC-205, TC-206).\n51\t- **WI-560 DW1** — ONE definition of \"the last commit that could invalidate a\n52\t  verdict\", used by the merge slot AND the C2 review-owed derivation. The\n53\t  double-identical-round class is now unrepresentable, not policed: the commits\n54\t  that caused it cannot move the identity either reader compares.\n55\t- **WI-559 DW2** — a committing ADJUDICATE session schedules its round exactly\n56\t  as a committing BUILD does, under the dial; the phase stays in\n57\t  `NON_BUILD_PHASES` because a judgement is not a build. No exit banner claims a\n58\t  round that was never drawn — it counts them.\n59\t- **The dial** — `docs/process.toml [attestation] adjudication_review`\n60\t  (`never` / `when-minting` / `always`; template and this repo ship\n61\t  `when-minting`), read through `agent_common.adjudication_review_owed` by BOTH\n62\t  the scheduler and the gate, with a closed vocabulary refused at preflight and\n63\t  a conservative fallback. Its `docs/enforcement-audit.md` row and the\n64\t  `RESYNC_PACK.md` entry ship with it. An adjudication lane drafting ordinary\n65\t  successors now merges with NO verdict artifact present anywhere — the OI-76\n66\t  acceptance becomes measurable on the next unattended run.\n67\t\n68\tReview A rework closed both evidence-boundary gaps. The loop's resume reader now\n69\tuses the same branch-scoped committed-path, logged-session and tree-bound entry\n70\tpipeline as the merge gate, so an approval-shaped file produced by a BUILD\n71\tsession cannot suppress the round the gate requires. The trailer's `rounds=N`\n72\tfield is now defined and checked as the completed review cycles represented at\n73\tthe governing tree (a dual-review cycle counts once, and rework starts the\n74\ttree-scoped count over); both the coordinator writer and gate derive that value\n75\tfrom the shared evidence. LLR-207's rationale now carries only the standing\n76\ttechnical reason, without the decision's provenance narrative.\n77\t\n78\t`LLR-140`'s Approved detail cell was re-pointed IN-LANE: it asserted the retired\n79\ttime comparison, which nothing detects once it is false. Ratchet bumps\n80\t(`agent_common` 1272→1305, `agent_loop` 2519→2578, `integrate` 1298→1382,\n81\t`check` 1163→1177, `bootstrap` 1658→1660, smoke membership 1480→1560) each carry\n82\ttheir reason at the entry; `_verdict_gate`'s complexity bump was REFUSED and the\n83\tfunction decomposed instead. Rework full suite: 3339 passed, 24 skipped, 1 failed\n84\tin 620.13s at `f418cba1` —\n85\tthe failure is `docs/stage` freshness, a trunk-lane artifact a work branch must\n86\tnot commit, bisected clean at the integration base. Account, deviations and the\n87\tone out-of-scope finding: `docs/log.d/WI-579-verdict-carrier-and-adjudication-review.md`.\n88\t\n89\t## Context\n90\t\n91\tMinted by the owner-directed backlog restructure of 2026-09-02 (plan of record `docs/plans/2026-09-02-backlog-restructure-and-consolidation.md` §2.2; executed out of band as a hand trunk commit series, not by a lane). The absorbed rows are archived under `docs/archive/work/restructured/` with their scope text untouched; their Done-when blocks are QUOTED below under their old ids and remain the spec this row must satisfy — decompose, don't paraphrase.\n92\t\n93\t**Why one row.** WI-558 Done-when 2 retires the gate's freshness comparison in\n94\tfavour of tree identity; WI-560 Done-when 1 builds one shared freshness\n95\tdefinition for the gate and the C2 review-owed derivation; WI-559 Done-when 2\n96\tmakes an ADJUDICATE commit schedule a round, which only means something once\n97\tthe round carrier WI-558 defines exists. Built apart in any order, the later\n98\tlane undoes part of the earlier one. Together: the gate and the review-owed\n99\tderivation read the SAME tree-identity trailer, and the round an adjudication\n100\towes is drawn u
