{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016mmYawu58hMftNSZSbbMQQ","type":"tool_result","content":"24:| \"Every declared test case passed\" is a HARNESS claim, never a cell or a hand-written file, and it expires with the tree it was measured on (OI-30 D2; WI-500) | Harness + Test (structural) | Was a VACUOUS guard — `DevStg-Release` was returned by nothing, so nothing could claim it falsely and nothing could claim it at all. Now the rung has exactly one input: `spine_stage(..., evidence_passed=)`, fed only by `kitlib.stage.evidence_verdict` over `docs/test/evidence`, which `record_test_evidence.py` writes only on a green harness exit (no flag records without running; no `outcome = fail` state; a partial `smoke` tier refused at the writer AND the reader). The claim is bound BY VALUE — a SHA-256 over the spine registries plus the declared `[paths]` source/test trees — so it cannot outlive its tree; and because the record is a declared stage input whose presence makes `stage.fingerprint` fold that same surface, a stale record reds `derive_stage --check` instead of sitting unread. The structural half is `tests/test_approval_level.py::test_the_RELEASE_rung_has_EXACTLY_ONE_PRODUCER_and_it_is_the_EVIDENCE_VERDICT`: exactly one Release return, guarded by the bare parameter, so a guard computed from Status cells is unrepresentable (driven against three mutants). **Honest residue:** this is not a signature — a determined author can compute a valid binding by hand. It defeats a green that outlived its tree, not forgery, and buying the stronger property would need a key and a verifier every adopter must manage |\n53:| A row states ONE verification method — its prose does not claim an instrument its `Verification` field contradicts | Harness (advisory) | Was **nothing**: the enum and the prose describe the same thing and no check compared them, so SR-052/SR-053 flipped `Critique`→`Test` on 2026-07-26 and went on demanding an APPROVE verdict from rubrics whose headers read RETIRED — three weeks, several reviews and a full re-tier pass at rc=0. Now `trace_text.verification_coherence_advisories` (warn-only, never the exit code; log `2026-08-16p`) over `Rationale` + `AcceptanceCriteria`. Two measured narrowings, both recorded in the docstring: `Requirement` is excluded (it fired on SR-040, where `CRITIQUE` names a routed session phase, not a verdict), and the rubric token is the bare word rather than a path (the path form missed all three real cases). One direction only — a `Critique` row naming no instrument is not reported, since its TC may legitimately hold the naming. Honest residue: detection is the token AS WRITTEN, so a cell describing a critique without the vocabulary passes |\n57:| A merged WI carries an INDEPENDENT fresh-context review verdict, and that verdict judged the tree being merged (RULING-7 under OI-76, ruled 2026-08-31) | Harness (ERROR) + Reviewer | Was a harness rung reading an artifact NOTHING WROTE: `integrate._verdict_gate` required `docs/reviews/WI-<n>-REVIEW-A.md`, every one in this repo's history was hand-compiled by a human sitting, and the file it demanded had no anti-forgery story at all — one line saying `VERDICT: APPROVE findings=0`, authored by anyone with commit access and no round behind it, cleared the rung, while the ROUND FILES that do carry provenance were ignored. Measured cost: the queue advanced one row per human intervention for nine hours on 2026-08-31, and a BUILD session had already written an approval-shaped file into its own review path. Now the gate computes over the round files `kitlib.verdict` reads, joined to the COORDINATOR's own committed session log — a file in `docs/reviews/` is a round only when `docs/iteration/<train>-<NNN>-*.log` declares a REVIEW phase, so an implementer cannot author its own round without also forging the loop's telemetry. Freshness is no longer a comparison but an IDENTITY: `tree_identity` folds the tree with `docs/reviews/`, `docs/log.d/` and `docs/iteration/` removed, and a verdict counts only while it names that value — which retires the ordering rule (a re-run round could silently promote a stale APPROVE) and makes the double-identical-round class unrepresentable rather than merely policed, since the commits that caused it cannot move the identity either reader compares. The `Review-Verdict: <word> rounds=<N> tree=<64 hex>` trailer is the machine half, verified against its carrier's own tree (the `Bar-Green` pattern) and read as a CROSS-CHECK — an attestation contradicting the rounds REFUSES the merge. **Honest residue, three-fold.** It is not a signature: anyone with commit access can write a trailer on their own commit and it will verify, which is exactly why the trailer is not an accept path and the session-log join is. The legacy hand-authored rollup still clears the gate for the length of the migration window (with a stderr WARN naming it), so the forgeable path is open until that window closes. And whether the reviewer actually reviewed — as opposed to writing `APPROVE findings=0` — is Reviewer-tier and always will be; what is mechanized is that a logged reviewer session produced a verdict over THIS tree |\n58:| Whether an ADJUDICATE lane owes a review round at all is a DECLARED policy, read identically by the scheduler and the gate (2026-09-02 restructure plan §3) | Harness (ERROR) + Test | Was a CONTRADICTION nothing detected: `ADJUDICATE` sat in `agent_loop.NON_BUILD_PHASES` so no round was ever scheduled after a judgement, while the gate demanded a verdict from every merged WI — so every adjudication merge was a supervisor stop, and three lanes on the 2026-08-31 run exited DONE reporting \"review round approved\" with no round drawn. Now `docs/process.toml [attestation] adjudication_review` (`never` / `when-minting` / `always`, shipped `when-minting`) is read through ONE function, `agent_common.adjudication_review_owed`, by both the round scheduler and `integrate._verdict_owed`, so the round the loop draws and the verdict the gate demands cannot come apart; the value is a CLOSED vocabulary refused at preflight, and an unreadable one falls to `when-minting` rather than to `never`. The banner counts the rounds it actually drew. **Honest residue:** the dial reads the DECLARED `safety_class` of the successors a verdict drafts, so a judgement that mints a spine-shaped row declared `ordinary` buys no round — the same declared-class exposure the batch admission carries, and caught after merge by the amendment trigger rather than before it |\n78:| A review finding is confirmed (reproduced) or refuted before code changes; a re-review round verifies fixes, never hunts fresh findings in them (WI-373) | Reviewer + Prose | process-options.md \"The LLM-gate verdict protocol\" (the finding lifecycle). Symmetric to the signed-measurements row: nothing mechanical can tell a reproduction from a recollection, so the round record holding the confirm/refute evidence is the enforcer; `score_reviews.py`'s confirmed-finding rate is the advisory backstop *on paper* — its scoreboard has been dark since 2026-07-15, and feed-or-delete is an open owner call (2026-07-28 audit rec #8). The evidence: rounds 127→131 ran ~70% non-product findings, and the self-aimed rounds converged to zero while manufacturing work |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a2a731ad-fd0c-4e02-bdd6-3eb62e37e416","uuid":"0521f54b-fec5-4930-aa90-ced4bb68e855","timestamp":"2026-09-03T03:47:45.332Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"24:| \"Every declared test case passed\" is a HARNESS claim, never a cell or a hand-written file, and it expires with the tree it was measured on (OI-30 D2; WI-500) | Harness + Test (structural) | Was a VACUOUS guard — `DevStg-Release` was returned by nothing, so nothing could claim it falsely and nothing could claim it at all. Now the rung has exactly one input: `spine_stage(..., evidence_passed=)`, fed only by `kitlib.stage.evidence_verdict` over `doc